	'k020e0d17' => '(sittings and house rules)',
	'k02887c55' => 'Between 14:30 and 18:00, Kohaku Brasserie does not close its doors. Instead, the tempo slows deliberately. Table linen is cleared from bare wooden tops, the music softens, and long afternoon sunlight cuts across the room. We offer our afternoon plate for €16, alongside freshly brewed coffee, tea, and warm pastries. No reservations are needed for parties of four or fewer; guests drop in to read, hold quiet conversations, or write at corner tables, finding a calm haven in the city center when most restaurant dining rooms are locked.',
	'k029b6cf8' => 'Service changes rhythm as the light shifts across the room. Midday brings brisk two-course lunches and full tables, while afternoon settles into quiet coffee, reading, and shared plates beside tall windows.',
