	'k0ffe715e' => 'Over the seasons, the Lantern Room has become home to enduring traditions. We warmly recall a Thursday lunch of six colleagues that became a monthly table, continuing year after year. We watched a 15:00 coffee meeting that ran smoothly into the late sitting as conversation deepened over wine. And on a memorable autumn evening, the room held a joyous wedding-eve dinner of 18, gathered under the soft glow of paper lanterns for shared plates, heartfelt toasts, and celebration late into the night.',
	'k11c4677b' => 'Head chef and co-founder Tomasz Lindqvist has defined Kohaku Brasserie’s culinary philosophy since 2014 with an emphasis on clarity and restraint. Sous chef Amara Osei directs daily service at the pass, ensuring impeccable execution across all line stations. Kenji Albrecht-Mori oversees pastry, bringing technical rigor to afternoon bakes, delicate lunch tarts, and comforting late-night desserts. Together, they guide a brigade committed to classical kitchen craft, working calmly under the heat lamps to plate each order with consistency and understated care.',
