	'k5bea705c' => 'Tell us the date, the sitting and the party size.',
	'k5d3f1a4c' => 'Six courses served at the eight counter seats directly overlooking the kitchen pass.',
	'k5e292257' => 'As the clock strikes 22:00, the bar becomes the focal point of our late sitting under gentle candle light. Guests seated at the counter can order from our dedicated late-sitting bar menu until kitchen last orders at 23:15. Offerings include warm house-cured meats, seasonal terrines, pickled market vegetables, and crusty bread with cultured butter. Paired with late-night wine pours and curated music by Daniel Okafor, the bar provides a calm, civilized retreat where night owls can savor unhurried food and drink until midnight.',
	'k5e706a9b' => 'Visit',
	'k5efb220b' => '(The counter)',
	'k5f9e6e1d' => '(The quiet hours)',
	'k6029659f' => 'Lunch begins at 11:30 with natural daylight filling the room. Tables fill with colleagues and neighbors ordering two-course and three-course set menus, featuring fresh market fish and crusty bread. The pace is steady and efficient for working midday schedules, yet relaxed enough for those wishing to linger over a glass of wine through the early afternoon.',
	'k6038f44f' => 'From 11:30 to 14:30 Tuesday through Saturday, our set lunch provides two courses for €28 or three courses for €34. The menu features light broths with seasonal herbs, pan-roasted market fish with steamed greens, and poached pear tart. During the quiet hours between 14:30 and 18:00, we serve our afternoon plate for €16, composed of warm sourdough, cultured butter, braised seasonal beans, and mature cheese. These daytime offerings give guests a focused, satisfying meal without fuss, whether stopping during a working lunch or taking a solitary break.',
	'k6082728b' => '(the people in the room)',
	'k64474197' => 'Many European brasseries historically served as all-day civic gathering points, a tradition Kohaku Brasserie deliberately preserves at 14 Arcade Row. A neighborhood lives across multiple tempos: early meetings, post-lunch work sessions, spontaneous late-afternoon reunions, and leisurely dinners. Splitting service into rigid shifts breaks that continuity. By keeping one room open continuously from 11:30 through midnight, we ensure our guests always have a dependable, warm table waiting for them, whether they arrive for an espresso at 15:00 or stay through until midnight dessert.',
	'k65034afa' => 'Behind the pass at Kohaku Brasserie, cooking is organized around three disciplined shift starts and seven key individuals. Every plate reflects meticulous preparation, collaborative timing, and respect for ingredients.',
	'k66ba7c9c' => 'We welcome dining guests across four distinct daily sittings: Lunch from 11:30 to 14:30, the quiet hours from 14:30 to 18:00, Dinner from 18:00 to 22:00, and our late sitting from 22:00 to 00:00, with kitchen last orders at 23:15. Our doors are open Tuesday through Saturday from 11:30 to midnight, and Sunday from 11:30 to 17:00. Mondays we are closed. Tables in the main dining room seat up to 6 guests, while bar seating accommodates solo diners and pairs.',
	'k6764b8e9' => 'Find us at 14 Arcade Row, Old Exchange Quarter, Lowmarket. Our dining room and bar operate Tuesday through Saturday from 11:30 to 00:00, and Sunday from 11:30 to 17:00. The brasserie is closed on Mondays. For reservations, general enquiries, or event planning, contact our team at bookings@kohaku-brasserie.example or telephone +00 20 7000 0414 during service hours. Whether dropping in for a glass of wine or attending a full dinner sitting, we are ready to assist you.',
	'k676da5d1' => 'The Room',
	'k69e430f7' => 'At Kohaku Brasserie, we believe communication should be as deliberate and thoughtful as our cooking. The Monday letter is sent once every Monday morning, directly to your inbox before our weekly service begins on Tuesday at 11:30. We never flood your inbox with daily promotions, marketing campaigns, or third-party announcements. Instead, it serves as a single quiet dispatch that shares what is inspiring our kitchen and dining room as the new week gets underway.',
	'k6a73a878' => 'Dinner à la carte',
	'k6aa545ff' => 'Dinner',
	'k6b39ac81' => '(introduction)',
	'k6d70c38e' => 'Afternoon plate and coffee; no booking for four or fewer.',
	'k6f3bf8be' => 'Can you visit the bar without a dinner reservation?',
	'k6f729726' => 'Arcade Row is a quiet pedestrian lane surfaced with heritage cobblestones. Guests traveling by public transit can arrive by tram, alighting at the central stop in the Old Exchange Quarter, which leaves you just a brief, pleasant walk from our front entrance. Dedicated bicycle stands are situated right along Arcade Row for cyclists. For guests arriving by car, several public parking garages are located within walking distance across the quarter, as Arcade Row itself remains closed to vehicular traffic.',
	'k6fa67673' => 'Who founded Kohaku Brasserie?',
