	'kafc73664' => 'The pass and the counter',
	'kb1a37cf6' => 'Reflections from our dining room, pass, and cellar.',
	'kb1e4186a' => 'At the back of the room sits the open pass, where head chef Tomasz Lindqvist and the brigade assemble every plate under focused heat lamps. Added in 2019, the 8 counter seats bring guests into close proximity with the rhythm of the kitchen line without interrupting its deliberate focus. From these high wooden stools, diners observe the disciplined choreography of pan, board, and seasoning, enjoying dishes handed across the counter the moment they are finished. It represents the active heart of the brasserie, bridging the craft of the kitchen directly with the life of the dining room.',
	'kb325c70b' => '(the bar)',
	'kb36c4e68' => 'Parties of 7 or more cannot be accommodated in the main room and must reserve the Lantern Room via email. For smaller groups and solitary guests, walk-ins are warmly welcomed without reservations during the quiet hours from 14:30 to 18:00 for afternoon plates or coffee. Please note that all reserved tables are held strictly for 15 minutes past the booking time. If you are delayed, notify us immediately by phone on +00 20 7000 0414 so our reception team can hold your table.',
	'kb4cd379a' => 'Night brings deep shadows, warm tungsten lamps, and candles flickering across white linen. Daniel Okafor leads service for late diners and evening arrivals seeking our three-course late-sitting menu. The kitchen continues cooking until last orders at 23:15, sending comforting dishes across the pass while Lucía Ferreira pours wine at the eight-seat bar until midnight closes the day.',
	'kb6111153' => '14 Arcade Row<br>Old Exchange Quarter, Lowmarket',
	'kb986f853' => 'Our kitchen prepares seasonal menus across four services each day, with all prices in euros including service.',
